   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "לֹא יֹאמַר לָהּ ״הֲרֵי כְּתוּבָּתִיךְ״. מַאי וְכֵן?",
   "en": "The mishna further stated that the yavam «may not say to her: Here is your marriage contract,» and similarly, a man may not make such a statement to his wife. Rather, all of his property is mortgaged for her marriage contract. The Gemara asks: «What» is the relevance of the phrase: «And similarly,» here? The halakha in both cases appears to be identical."
  }
